{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789803817955,"sessionID":"ses_f47618eddffeaN425WAlenRz9Q","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_b2a30322ccc94ed290595ac6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/tmp/opencode/dogfood/D3-ON-1/work/crates/mcp-server/src/integration.rs","limit":420},"output":"<path>/tmp/opencode/dogfood/D3-ON-1/work/crates/mcp-server/src/integration.rs</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: //! CodeBro P8 — OpenCode integration layer.\n2: //!\n3: //! P8 makes CodeBro a *natural* engineering context/runtime companion for\n4: //! OpenCode (and any MCP agent client) without moving any execution,\n5: //! reasoning, or agent-loop ownership into CodeBro. It is a thin\n6: //! integration-contract layer over the mature P0–P7 core:\n7: //!\n8: //! - **Contract surface:** the existing 24 MCP tools ARE the contract.\n9: //!   `engineering_brief` is the primary high-level context surface — including\n10: //!   bounded impact evidence, which the brief assembles internally via the\n11: //!   impact engine (the standalone `impact_analyze` tool was removed after\n12: //!   measurement showed zero agent use across 19 sessions; see\n13: //!   eval/IMPACT_ANALYZE_REMOVAL_PROPOSAL.md);\n14: //!   `context` the always-available packet; `recall`/`engineering_facts`/\n15: //!   `repository_health` targeted follow-up; `remember`/\n16: //!   `record_memory`/`task`/`learn`/`skill` the explicit persistence path.\n17: //!   P8 adds NO new tools — every capability already exists.\n18: //! - **Protocol hygiene:** a stdio MCP server must keep stdout reserved\n19: //!   for JSON-RPC. `tracing` therefore writes to **stderr** (see `lib.rs`\n20: //!   — the subscriber is built with `.with_writer(std::io::stderr)`).\n21: //!   Before P8, log lines were emitted to stdout, corrupting the framing\n22: //!   channel (observed live: an ERROR line interleaved with responses).\n23: //! - **Server identity:** the initialize response identifies the server\n24: //!   as `codebro` with the crate version (not rmcp's `from_build_env`\n25: //!   default, which reported `\"rmcp\"` — a real discovery/telemetry defect\n26: //!   for clients that display or route on server identity).\n27: //! - **Client observability (bounded, privacy-preserving):** the client's\n28: //!   declared `clientInfo` (name + version) is captured at initialize and\n29: //!   emitted as a tracing event; every tool call emits a one-line tracing\n30: //!   event (client, tool, duration, error status, response bytes). Never\n31: //!   logged: tool arguments, task text, brief content, secrets. The client\n32: //!   name is *not* persisted anywhere — it is process-local observability.\n33: //! - **Degraded mode contract:** every read tool already degrades to\n34: //!   explicit unknowns (P6/P7 failure model). For the *client* side the\n35: //!   contract is: CodeBro unavailable → OpenCode continues with its own\n36: //!   native tools; CodeBro stale → briefs carry `STALE_INDEX`; CodeBro\n37: //!   unknown → explicit `UNKNOWN` entries. This module documents that\n38: //!   contract; the guarantees are enforced by the P0–P7 tools themselves.\n39: //!\n40: //! Boundary (unchanged from P0–P7): OpenCode decides WHEN context is\n41: //! needed; CodeBro decides WHAT context is relevant; CodeBro persists\n42: //! meaningful engineering knowledge only through explicit write tools\n43: //! with the unchanged authority gates (`user_confirmed` speech acts,\n44: //! evidence-cited inference, store-enforced lifecycle).\n45: //!\n46: //! No agent loop, no scheduler, no daemon, no watcher, no model calls, no\n47: //! skill execution, no remote transport — request-driven only, exactly\n48: //! like P0–P7.\n49: \n50: #![allow(dead_code, unused_imports)] // deliberate product surface beyond current callers; revisit at legacy retirement\n51: \n52: use std::time::Instant;\n53: \n54: /// Human-readable server identity for the MCP `initialize` handshake.\n55: ///\n56: /// Clients (OpenCode among them) display and sometimes route on\n57: /// `serverInfo.name`. Reporting the SDK default (`\"rmcp\"`) made every\n58: /// CodeBro instance masquerade as the transport library; P8 reports the\n59: /// product identity. The version is the crate version from the build\n60: /// environment.\n61: pub const SERVER_NAME: &str = \"codebro\";\n62: \n63: /// One-line-per-tool-call observability record.\n64: ///\n65: /// Deliberately minimal: client identity, tool name, duration, error\n66: /// status, and response size. **Never** arguments, task text, brief\n67: /// content, or anything secret-shaped — this exists so integrators can\n68: /// diagnose \"is the MCP server being called, is it fast, is it failing\"\n69: /// from stderr logs without becoming a data-leak path (see the P8\n70: /// observability contract).\n71: #[derive(Debug, Clone)]\n72: pub struct ToolCallObservation {\n73:     /// Client-declared name from `initialize` (e.g. \"opencode\"), when known.\n74:     pub client_name: Option<String>,\n75:     /// Client-declared version from `initialize`, when known.\n76:     pub client_version: Option<String>,\n77:     /// Tool name exactly as routed.\n78:     pub tool: String,\n79:     /// Wall-clock execution duration.\n80:     pub duration_ms: u128,\n81:     /// Whether the call completed with an error (JSON-RPC error OR\n82:     /// `isError` tool result).\n83:     pub errored: bool,\n84:     /// Error label when errored (code/message summary, bounded, redacted).\n85:     pub error_summary: Option<String>,\n86:     /// Serialized response size in bytes (bounded evidence of bounds).\n87:     pub response_bytes: usize,\n88: }\n89: \n90: impl ToolCallObservation {\n91:     /// Render the single-line tracing form. Bounded (each field capped),\n92:     /// secret-redacted through the same authority every other free-text\n93:     /// seam uses — defense in depth, even though only tool names and\n94:     /// client names (bounded vocabulary) flow here.\n95:     pub fn render_line(&self) -> String {\n96:         let client = match (&self.client_name, &self.client_version) {\n97:             (Some(n), Some(v)) => format!(\"{}/{}\", redact(n), redact(v)),\n98:             (Some(n), None) => redact(n).to_string(),\n99:             (None, _) => \"unknown\".to_string(),\n100:         };\n101:         let status = if self.errored {\n102:             match &self.error_summary {\n103:                 Some(s) => format!(\"error: {}\", redact(s)),\n104:                 None => \"error\".to_string(),\n105:             }\n106:         } else {\n107:             \"ok\".to_string()\n108:         };\n109:         format!(\n110:             \"client={} tool={} duration_ms={} status={} response_bytes={}\",\n111:             client, self.tool, self.duration_ms, status, self.response_bytes\n112:         )\n113:     }\n114: }\n115: \n116: /// Redact through the canonical authority (defense in depth; tool/client\n117: /// names are bounded vocabularies but the seam must never become the\n118: /// exception).\n119: fn redact(s: &str) -> String {\n120:     crate::tools::shell::redact_secrets_public(s)\n121: }\n122: \n123: /// Measure a tool call for observability. Returns the observation for the\n124: /// caller to emit after the response is known (the caller owns the\n125: /// `Instant` lifecycle because it also owns the response envelope).\n126: pub fn observe_call(\n127:     client: Option<(String, String)>,\n128:     tool: &str,\n129:     started: Instant,\n130:     errored: bool,\n131:     error_summary: Option<String>,\n132:     response_bytes: usize,\n133: ) -> ToolCallObservation {\n134:     ToolCallObservation {\n135:         client_name: client.as_ref().map(|(n, _)| n.clone()),\n136:         client_version: client.as_ref().map(|(_, v)| v.clone()),\n137:         tool: tool.to_string(),\n138:         duration_ms: started.elapsed().as_millis(),\n139:         errored,\n140:         error_summary,\n141:         response_bytes,\n142:     }\n143: }\n144: \n145: /// Bound an error summary for the observation line (never a raw payload).\n146: pub fn bounded_error_summary(msg: &str) -> String {\n147:     let redacted = redact(msg);\n148:     redacted.chars().take(240).collect()\n149: }\n150: \n151: /// The P8 integration contract, expressed as data for tests and docs.\n152: ///\n153: /// Codifies what the 24 existing tools mean *to an agent client* so the\n154: /// contract is enforceable by regression tests instead of existing only\n155: /// in prose. Every entry maps an agent-client intent to the exact tool\n156: /// that serves it — the point of P8 §6 (\"avoid the client manually calling\n157: /// dozens of low-level tools\": the brief IS the primary surface, targeted\n158: /// follow-up uses existing semantic tools).\n159: pub mod contract {\n160:     /// The primary high-level context surface: one bounded, deterministic\n161:     /// brief covering repository identity, freshness, files, symbols,\n162:     /// dependencies, impact, tests, health, history, memory, learning,\n163:     /// skill applicability, task state, constraints, decisions, risks,\n164:     /// and explicit unknowns.\n165:     pub const PRIMARY_CONTEXT_TOOL: &str = \"engineering_brief\";\n166:     /// Always-available orientation packet (structural digest when no\n167:     /// task is known).\n168:     pub const ORIENTATION_TOOL: &str = \"context\";\n169:     /// Workspace-level orientation + fact counts + freshness.\n170:     pub const WORKSPACE_ORIENTATION_TOOL: &str = \"workspace_context\";\n171:     /// Targeted follow-up: verified repository facts.\n172:     pub const FACTS_TOOL: &str = \"engineering_facts\";\n173:     /// Targeted follow-up: structural impact of a change, served by the\n174:     /// brief's embedded bounded traversal (the standalone `impact_analyze`\n175:     /// tool was removed for non-use; the engine remains inside the brief).\n176:     pub const IMPACT_TOOL: &str = \"engineering_brief\";\n177:     /// Targeted follow-up: historical evidence (decisions/failures).\n178:     pub const HISTORY_TOOL: &str = \"recall\";\n179:     /// Targeted follow-up: engineering memory resolution.\n180:     pub const MEMORY_TOOL: &str = \"engineering_memory\";\n181:     /// Targeted follow-up: workspace health.\n182:     pub const HEALTH_TOOL: &str = \"repository_health\";\n183:     /// Durable task state (create/start/checkpoint/complete/…).\n184:     pub const TASK_TOOL: &str = \"task\";\n185:     /// Explicit user-confirmed preference/intent persistence.\n186:     pub const REMEMBER_TOOL: &str = \"remember\";\n187:     /// Durable agent-recorded engineering memory.\n188:     pub const RECORD_MEMORY_TOOL: &str = \"record_memory\";\n189:     /// Learning lifecycle (hypotheses from history; never self-confirmed).\n190:     pub const LEARN_TOOL: &str = \"learn\";\n191:     /// Skill lifecycle (CodeBro manages; OpenCode executes natively).\n192:     pub const SKILL_TOOL: &str = \"skill\";\n193:     /// Index refresh (freshness recovery path).\n194:     pub const REINDEX_TOOL: &str = \"reindex\";\n195: \n196:     /// The full P8 client-facing contract: intent → tool. Ordered by the\n197:     /// canonical acquisition flow (orientation → brief → targeted →\n198:     /// persistence). Regression tests assert each tool exists in the\n199:     /// router and the map covers exactly the capabilities P8 promises.\n200:     pub fn intents() -> &'static [(&'static str, &'static str)] {\n201:         &[\n202:             (\"primary_context\", PRIMARY_CONTEXT_TOOL),\n203:             (\"orientation\", ORIENTATION_TOOL),\n204:             (\"workspace_orientation\", WORKSPACE_ORIENTATION_TOOL),\n205:             (\"facts\", FACTS_TOOL),\n206:             (\"impact\", IMPACT_TOOL),\n207:             (\"history\", HISTORY_TOOL),\n208:             (\"memory\", MEMORY_TOOL),\n209:             (\"health\", HEALTH_TOOL),\n210:             (\"task_state\", TASK_TOOL),\n211:             (\"remember\", REMEMBER_TOOL),\n212:             (\"record_memory\", RECORD_MEMORY_TOOL),\n213:             (\"learn\", LEARN_TOOL),\n214:             (\"skill_lifecycle\", SKILL_TOOL),\n215:             (\"reindex\", REINDEX_TOOL),\n216:         ]\n217:     }\n218: }\n219: \n220: #[cfg(test)]\n221: mod tests {\n222:     use super::*;\n223: \n224:     #[test]\n225:     fn observation_line_is_bounded_and_redacted() {\n226:         let obs = ToolCallObservation {\n227:             client_name: Some(\"opencode\".into()),\n228:             client_version: Some(\"1.18.29\".into()),\n229:             tool: \"engineering_brief\".into(),\n230:             duration_ms: 42,\n231:             errored: false,\n232:             error_summary: None,\n233:             response_bytes: 8192,\n234:         };\n235:         let line = obs.render_line();\n236:         assert!(line.contains(\"client=opencode/1.18.29\"));\n237:         assert!(line.contains(\"tool=engineering_brief\"));\n238:         assert!(line.contains(\"status=ok\"));\n239:         assert!(!line.contains(\"task\"), \"no task text in observation\");\n240:         assert!(!line.contains(\"sk-\"), \"no secret-shaped text\");\n241:     }\n242: \n243:     #[test]\n244:     fn observation_line_redacts_secret_shaped_client_names() {\n245:         // Defense in depth: even if a hostile client declares a\n246:         // secret-shaped name, the observation never echoes it.\n247:         let obs = ToolCallObservation {\n248:             client_name: Some(\"sk-abc123secretkey\".into()),\n249:             client_version: None,\n250:             tool: \"workspace_context\".into(),\n251:             duration_ms: 1,\n252:             errored: true,\n253:             error_summary: Some(\"boom at sk-live-xyz\".into()),\n254:             response_bytes: 10,\n255:         };\n256:         let line = obs.render_line();\n257:         assert!(\n258:             !line.contains(\"sk-abc123secretkey\"),\n259:             \"client name must be redacted\"\n260:         );\n261:         assert!(!line.contains(\"sk-live-xyz\"), \"error must be redacted\");\n262:         assert!(line.contains(\"status=error\"));\n263:     }\n264: \n265:     #[test]\n266:     fn observation_line_handles_unknown_client() {\n267:         let obs = ToolCallObservation {\n268:             client_name: None,\n269:             client_version: None,\n270:             tool: \"memory_stats\".into(),\n271:             duration_ms: 0,\n272:             errored: false,\n273:             error_summary: None,\n274:             response_bytes: 0,\n275:         };\n276:         let line = obs.render_line();\n277:         assert!(line.contains(\"client=unknown\"));\n278:     }\n279: \n280:     #[test]\n281:     fn bounded_error_summary_truncates_and_redacts() {\n282:         let long = format!(\"{} {}\", \"x\".repeat(500), \"password=hunter2\");\n283:         let bounded = bounded_error_summary(&long);\n284:         assert!(bounded.chars().count() <= 240);\n285:         assert!(!bounded.contains(\"hunter2\"));\n286:     }\n287: \n288:     #[test]\n289:     fn contract_intents_cover_the_p8_flow_without_new_tools() {\n290:         let intents = contract::intents();\n291:         // Every intent maps to one of the existing 24 tools — P8 adds none.\n292:         for (_, tool) in intents {\n293:             assert!(\n294:                 matches!(\n295:                     *tool,\n296:                     \"engineering_brief\"\n297:                         | \"context\"\n298:                         | \"workspace_context\"\n299:                         | \"engineering_facts\"\n300:                         | \"recall\"\n301:                         | \"engineering_memory\"\n302:                         | \"repository_health\"\n303:                         | \"task\"\n304:                         | \"remember\"\n305:                         | \"record_memory\"\n306:                         | \"learn\"\n307:                         | \"skill\"\n308:                         | \"reindex\"\n309:                 ),\n310:                 \"contract tool {tool} is not an existing P0-P7 tool\"\n311:             );\n312:         }\n313:         // The primary surface is the brief — the P8 acquisition contract.\n314:         assert_eq!(contract::PRIMARY_CONTEXT_TOOL, \"engineering_brief\");\n315:         // No contract intent references a CRUD/second context system.\n316:         assert!(!intents.iter().any(|(_, t)| t.contains(\"get_\")));\n317:     }\n318: \n319:     #[test]\n320:     fn server_identity_is_the_product_not_the_sdk() {\n321:         assert_eq!(SERVER_NAME, \"codebro\");\n322:     }\n323: }\n\n(End of file - total 323 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"//! CodeBro P8 — OpenCode integration layer.\n//!\n//! P8 makes CodeBro a *natural* engineering context/runtime companion for\n//! OpenCode (and any MCP agent client) without moving any execution,\n//! reasoning, or agent-loop ownership into CodeBro. It is a thin\n//! integration-contract layer over the mature P0–P7 core:\n//!\n//! - **Contract surface:** the existing 24 MCP tools ARE the contract.\n//!   `engineering_brief` is the primary high-level context surface — including\n//!   bounded impact evidence, which the brief assembles internally via the\n//!   impact engine (the standalone `impact_analyze` tool was removed after\n//!   measurement showed zero agent use across 19 sessions; see\n//!   eval/IMPACT_ANALYZE_REMOVAL_PROPOSAL.md);\n//!   `context` the always-available packet; `recall`/`engineering_facts`/\n//!   `repository_health` targeted follow-up; `remember`/\n//!   `record_memory`/`task`/`learn`/`skill` the explicit persistence path.\n//!   P8 adds NO new tools — every capability already exists.\n//! - **Protocol hygiene:** a stdio MCP server must keep stdout reserved\n//!   for JSON-RPC. `tracing` therefore writes to **stderr** (see `lib.rs`\n//!   — the subscriber is built with `.with_writer(std::io::stderr)`).","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/tmp/opencode/dogfood/D3-ON-1/work/crates/mcp-server/src/integration.rs","text":"//! CodeBro P8 — OpenCode integration layer.\n//!\n//! P8 makes CodeBro a *natural* engineering context/runtime companion for\n//! OpenCode (and any MCP agent client) without moving any execution,\n//! reasoning, or agent-loop ownership into CodeBro. It is a thin\n//! integration-contract layer over the mature P0–P7 core:\n//!\n//! - **Contract surface:** the existing 24 MCP tools ARE the contract.\n//!   `engineering_brief` is the primary high-level context surface — including\n//!   bounded impact evidence, which the brief assembles internally via the\n//!   impact engine (the standalone `impact_analyze` tool was removed after\n//!   measurement showed zero agent use across 19 sessions; see\n//!   eval/IMPACT_ANALYZE_REMOVAL_PROPOSAL.md);\n//!   `context` the always-available packet; `recall`/`engineering_facts`/\n//!   `repository_health` targeted follow-up; `remember`/\n//!   `record_memory`/`task`/`learn`/`skill` the explicit persistence path.\n//!   P8 adds NO new tools — every capability already exists.\n//! - **Protocol hygiene:** a stdio MCP server must keep stdout reserved\n//!   for JSON-RPC. `tracing` therefore writes to **stderr** (see `lib.rs`\n//!   — the subscriber is built with `.with_writer(std::io::stderr)`).\n//!   Before P8, log lines were emitted to stdout, corrupting the framing\n//!   channel (observed live: an ERROR line interleaved with responses).\n//! - **Server identity:** the initialize response identifies the server\n//!   as `codebro` with the crate version (not rmcp's `from_build_env`\n//!   default, which reported `\"rmcp\"` — a real discovery/telemetry defect\n//!   for clients that display or route on server identity).\n//! - **Client observability (bounded, privacy-preserving):** the client's\n//!   declared `clientInfo` (name + version) is captured at initialize and\n//!   emitted as a tracing event; every tool call emits a one-line tracing\n//!   event (client, tool, duration, error status, response bytes). Never\n//!   logged: tool arguments, task text, brief content, secrets. The client\n//!   name is *not* persisted anywhere — it is process-local observability.\n//! - **Degraded mode contract:** every read tool already degrades to\n//!   explicit unknowns (P6/P7 failure model). For the *client* side the\n//!   contract is: CodeBro unavailable → OpenCode continues with its own\n//!   native tools; CodeBro stale → briefs carry `STALE_INDEX`; CodeBro\n//!   unknown → explicit `UNKNOWN` entries. This module documents that\n//!   contract; the guarantees are enforced by the P0–P7 tools themselves.\n//!\n//! Boundary (unchanged from P0–P7): OpenCode decides WHEN context is\n//! needed; CodeBro decides WHAT context is relevant; CodeBro persists\n//! meaningful engineering knowledge only through explicit write tools\n//! with the unchanged authority gates (`user_confirmed` speech acts,\n//! evidence-cited inference, store-enforced lifecycle).\n//!\n//! No agent loop, no scheduler, no daemon, no watcher, no model calls, no\n//! skill execution, no remote transport — request-driven only, exactly\n//! like P0–P7.\n\n#![allow(dead_code, unused_imports)] // deliberate product surface beyond current callers; revisit at legacy retirement\n\nuse std::time::Instant;\n\n/// Human-readable server identity for the MCP `initialize` handshake.\n///\n/// Clients (OpenCode among them) display and sometimes route on\n/// `serverInfo.name`. Reporting the SDK default (`\"rmcp\"`) made every\n/// CodeBro instance masquerade as the transport library; P8 reports the\n/// product identity. The version is the crate version from the build\n/// environment.\npub const SERVER_NAME: &str = \"codebro\";\n\n/// One-line-per-tool-call observability record.\n///\n/// Deliberately minimal: client identity, tool name, duration, error\n/// status, and response size. **Never** arguments, task text, brief\n/// content, or anything secret-shaped — this exists so integrators can\n/// diagnose \"is the MCP server being called, is it fast, is it failing\"\n/// from stderr logs without becoming a data-leak path (see the P8\n/// observability contract).\n#[derive(Debug, Clone)]\npub struct ToolCallObservation {\n    /// Client-declared name from `initialize` (e.g. \"opencode\"), when known.\n    pub client_name: Option<String>,\n    /// Client-declared version from `initialize`, when known.\n    pub client_version: Option<String>,\n    /// Tool name exactly as routed.\n    pub tool: String,\n    /// Wall-clock execution duration.\n    pub duration_ms: u128,\n    /// Whether the call completed with an error (JSON-RPC error OR\n    /// `isError` tool result).\n    pub errored: bool,\n    /// Error label when errored (code/message summary, bounded, redacted).\n    pub error_summary: Option<String>,\n    /// Serialized response size in bytes (bounded evidence of bounds).\n    pub response_bytes: usize,\n}\n\nimpl ToolCallObservation {\n    /// Render the single-line tracing form. Bounded (each field capped),\n    /// secret-redacted through the same authority every other free-text\n    /// seam uses — defense in depth, even though only tool names and\n    /// client names (bounded vocabulary) flow here.\n    pub fn render_line(&self) -> String {\n        let client = match (&self.client_name, &self.client_version) {\n            (Some(n), Some(v)) => format!(\"{}/{}\", redact(n), redact(v)),\n            (Some(n), None) => redact(n).to_string(),\n            (None, _) => \"unknown\".to_string(),\n        };\n        let status = if self.errored {\n            match &self.error_summary {\n                Some(s) => format!(\"error: {}\", redact(s)),\n                None => \"error\".to_string(),\n            }\n        } else {\n            \"ok\".to_string()\n        };\n        format!(\n            \"client={} tool={} duration_ms={} status={} response_bytes={}\",\n            client, self.tool, self.duration_ms, status, self.response_bytes\n        )\n    }\n}\n\n/// Redact through the canonical authority (defense in depth; tool/client\n/// names are bounded vocabularies but the seam must never become the\n/// exception).\nfn redact(s: &str) -> String {\n    crate::tools::shell::redact_secrets_public(s)\n}\n\n/// Measure a tool call for observability. Returns the observation for the\n/// caller to emit after the response is known (the caller owns the\n/// `Instant` lifecycle because it also owns the response envelope).\npub fn observe_call(\n    client: Option<(String, String)>,\n    tool: &str,\n    started: Instant,\n    errored: bool,\n    error_summary: Option<String>,\n    response_bytes: usize,\n) -> ToolCallObservation {\n    ToolCallObservation {\n        client_name: client.as_ref().map(|(n, _)| n.clone()),\n        client_version: client.as_ref().map(|(_, v)| v.clone()),\n        tool: tool.to_string(),\n        duration_ms: started.elapsed().as_millis(),\n        errored,\n        error_summary,\n        response_bytes,\n    }\n}\n\n/// Bound an error summary for the observation line (never a raw payload).\npub fn bounded_error_summary(msg: &str) -> String {\n    let redacted = redact(msg);\n    redacted.chars().take(240).collect()\n}\n\n/// The P8 integration contract, expressed as data for tests and docs.\n///\n/// Codifies what the 24 existing tools mean *to an agent client* so the\n/// contract is enforceable by regression tests instead of existing only\n/// in prose. Every entry maps an agent-client intent to the exact tool\n/// that serves it — the point of P8 §6 (\"avoid the client manually calling\n/// dozens of low-level tools\": the brief IS the primary surface, targeted\n/// follow-up uses existing semantic tools).\npub mod contract {\n    /// The primary high-level context surface: one bounded, deterministic\n    /// brief covering repository identity, freshness, files, symbols,\n    /// dependencies, impact, tests, health, history, memory, learning,\n    /// skill applicability, task state, constraints, decisions, risks,\n    /// and explicit unknowns.\n    pub const PRIMARY_CONTEXT_TOOL: &str = \"engineering_brief\";\n    /// Always-available orientation packet (structural digest when no\n    /// task is known).\n    pub const ORIENTATION_TOOL: &str = \"context\";\n    /// Workspace-level orientation + fact counts + freshness.\n    pub const WORKSPACE_ORIENTATION_TOOL: &str = \"workspace_context\";\n    /// Targeted follow-up: verified repository facts.\n    pub const FACTS_TOOL: &str = \"engineering_facts\";\n    /// Targeted follow-up: structural impact of a change, served by the\n    /// brief's embedded bounded traversal (the standalone `impact_analyze`\n    /// tool was removed for non-use; the engine remains inside the brief).\n    pub const IMPACT_TOOL: &str = \"engineering_brief\";\n    /// Targeted follow-up: historical evidence (decisions/failures).\n    pub const HISTORY_TOOL: &str = \"recall\";\n    /// Targeted follow-up: engineering memory resolution.\n    pub const MEMORY_TOOL: &str = \"engineering_memory\";\n    /// Targeted follow-up: workspace health.\n    pub const HEALTH_TOOL: &str = \"repository_health\";\n    /// Durable task state (create/start/checkpoint/complete/…).\n    pub const TASK_TOOL: &str = \"task\";\n    /// Explicit user-confirmed preference/intent persistence.\n    pub const REMEMBER_TOOL: &str = \"remember\";\n    /// Durable agent-recorded engineering memory.\n    pub const RECORD_MEMORY_TOOL: &str = \"record_memory\";\n    /// Learning lifecycle (hypotheses from history; never self-confirmed).\n    pub const LEARN_TOOL: &str = \"learn\";\n    /// Skill lifecycle (CodeBro manages; OpenCode executes natively).\n    pub const SKILL_TOOL: &str = \"skill\";\n    /// Index refresh (freshness recovery path).\n    pub const REINDEX_TOOL: &str = \"reindex\";\n\n    /// The full P8 client-facing contract: intent → tool. Ordered by the\n    /// canonical acquisition flow (orientation → brief → targeted →\n    /// persistence). Regression tests assert each tool exists in the\n    /// router and the map covers exactly the capabilities P8 promises.\n    pub fn intents() -> &'static [(&'static str, &'static str)] {\n        &[\n            (\"primary_context\", PRIMARY_CONTEXT_TOOL),\n            (\"orientation\", ORIENTATION_TOOL),\n            (\"workspace_orientation\", WORKSPACE_ORIENTATION_TOOL),\n            (\"facts\", FACTS_TOOL),\n            (\"impact\", IMPACT_TOOL),\n            (\"history\", HISTORY_TOOL),\n            (\"memory\", MEMORY_TOOL),\n            (\"health\", HEALTH_TOOL),\n            (\"task_state\", TASK_TOOL),\n            (\"remember\", REMEMBER_TOOL),\n            (\"record_memory\", RECORD_MEMORY_TOOL),\n            (\"learn\", LEARN_TOOL),\n            (\"skill_lifecycle\", SKILL_TOOL),\n            (\"reindex\", REINDEX_TOOL),\n        ]\n    }\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {\n    use super::*;\n\n    #[test]\n    fn observation_line_is_bounded_and_redacted() {\n        let obs = ToolCallObservation {\n            client_name: Some(\"opencode\".into()),\n            client_version: Some(\"1.18.29\".into()),\n            tool: \"engineering_brief\".into(),\n            duration_ms: 42,\n            errored: false,\n            error_summary: None,\n            response_bytes: 8192,\n        };\n        let line = obs.render_line();\n        assert!(line.contains(\"client=opencode/1.18.29\"));\n        assert!(line.contains(\"tool=engineering_brief\"));\n        assert!(line.contains(\"status=ok\"));\n        assert!(!line.contains(\"task\"), \"no task text in observation\");\n        assert!(!line.contains(\"sk-\"), \"no secret-shaped text\");\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn observation_line_redacts_secret_shaped_client_names() {\n        // Defense in depth: even if a hostile client declares a\n        // secret-shaped name, the observation never echoes it.\n        let obs = ToolCallObservation {\n            client_name: Some(\"sk-abc123secretkey\".into()),\n            client_version: None,\n            tool: \"workspace_context\".into(),\n            duration_ms: 1,\n            errored: true,\n            error_summary: Some(\"boom at sk-live-xyz\".into()),\n            response_bytes: 10,\n        };\n        let line = obs.render_line();\n        assert!(\n            !line.contains(\"sk-abc123secretkey\"),\n            \"client name must be redacted\"\n        );\n        assert!(!line.contains(\"sk-live-xyz\"), \"error must be redacted\");\n        assert!(line.contains(\"status=error\"));\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn observation_line_handles_unknown_client() {\n        let obs = ToolCallObservation {\n            client_name: None,\n            client_version: None,\n            tool: \"memory_stats\".into(),\n            duration_ms: 0,\n            errored: false,\n            error_summary: None,\n            response_bytes: 0,\n        };\n        let line = obs.render_line();\n        assert!(line.contains(\"client=unknown\"));\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn bounded_error_summary_truncates_and_redacts() {\n        let long = format!(\"{} {}\", \"x\".repeat(500), \"password=hunter2\");\n        let bounded = bounded_error_summary(&long);\n        assert!(bounded.chars().count() <= 240);\n        assert!(!bounded.contains(\"hunter2\"));\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn contract_intents_cover_the_p8_flow_without_new_tools() {\n        let intents = contract::intents();\n        // Every intent maps to one of the existing 24 tools — P8 adds none.\n        for (_, tool) in intents {\n            assert!(\n                matches!(\n                    *tool,\n                    \"engineering_brief\"\n                        | \"context\"\n                        | \"workspace_context\"\n                        | \"engineering_facts\"\n                        | \"recall\"\n                        | \"engineering_memory\"\n                        | \"repository_health\"\n                        | \"task\"\n                        | \"remember\"\n                        | \"record_memory\"\n                        | \"learn\"\n                        | \"skill\"\n                        | \"reindex\"\n                ),\n                \"contract tool {tool} is not an existing P0-P7 tool\"\n            );\n        }\n        // The primary surface is the brief — the P8 acquisition contract.\n        assert_eq!(contract::PRIMARY_CONTEXT_TOOL, \"engineering_brief\");\n        // No contract intent references a CRUD/second context system.\n        assert!(!intents.iter().any(|(_, t)| t.contains(\"get_\")));\n    }\n\n    #[test]\n    fn server_identity_is_the_product_not_the_sdk() {\n        assert_eq!(SERVER_NAME, \"codebro\");\n    }\n}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":323,"totalLines":323,"truncated":false}},"title":"crates/mcp-server/src/integration.rs","time":{"start":1789803817940,"end":1789803817950}},"id":"prt_0b89eea13001WUu7MXGCRmMDnh","sessionID":"ses_f47618eddffeaN425WAlenRz9Q","messageID":"msg_0b89eac69001FFt4H6u9XcN801"}}
